course: dictionary
lesson: 9436
title: Stainless: without stains or marks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word stainless is built from two parts. Stain is a mark that is hard to remove, and -less means without. So stainless means without stains or marks. You can check this by swapping the meaning into a sentence.
explain: Read the context: «Carbon steel knives (not stainless) get dark spots when left wet with acid such as vinegar, so chefs dry them at once.» The brackets set carbon steel against stainless. Carbon steel gets dark spots, so stainless steel does not. Swap in your meaning: stainless steel is steel without spots. It fits.
explain: The same word can describe a person's good name. A stainless record means a history with no bad deeds in it. Read the words around the word to see which meaning fits: is the thing being described a metal, or a person's reputation?
fact: Stainless means without stains or marks.
fact: Stainless steel is a mixture of metals, including chromium, that does not rust or stain easily.
fact: Stainless steel is used for cutlery, sinks, pans and hospital tools because it is easy to clean.
fact: In stories, «a stainless record» means a spotless, good reputation with no bad deeds.
fact: Stainless steel and a stainless record are common phrases to remember.
exercise: «Carbon steel knives (not stainless) get dark spots when left wet with acid such as vinegar.» What does stainless mean here? | Full of vinegar | *Without stains or marks | Made of wood | Very sharp
exercise: Why do chefs like stainless steel for pans and knives? | It is soft and bends easily | It makes the pan heavy and loud | It stops food from cooking | *It is easy to clean and does not rust easily
exercise: «She had a stainless record and was trusted by everyone.» What does stainless mean here? | A record made of steel | A record that is very loud | A record with dark spots | *A clean history with no bad deeds
test: In «Carbon steel knives (not stainless) get dark spots», which steel gets the dark spots? | Chromium | Stainless steel | *Carbon steel | Vinegar
test: Stainless steel is a mixture that includes which metal? | Lead | Silver | Gold | *Chromium
exam: What is the best meaning of stainless in «a stainless record»? | Full of stains | *Spotless, with no bad deeds | Rusty and old | Very noisy
